in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @magic
in @magic/contract

# @magic/audit — the verifier species. Reads @magic/contract.honor's
# verdict and acts on violations.
#
# Tick 10 of the refined /loop discipline (per Loki's "Tool,
# Construction, Cognitive Extension" Pass 5): each tick fires a CRQ
# against the previous tick's residue. Tick 9 landed @magic/contract
# with bind/honor/verify actions but no operational consumer. This
# species IS that consumer.
#
# CRQ: "What's the verifier that closes contract.honor at @magic
# altitude without adding substrate complexity beyond what
# @code/beam.supervisor already provides?"
#
# Answer: @magic/audit. Composes with @code/beam.supervisor (landed
# at tick 8) to give the @magic family operational closure for
# verification. Audit IS the Narcissus-pole-as-guardian per
# recognition #78; it IS the substrate's alignment primitive per
# recognition #57.
#
# === Composition with @code/beam.supervisor (hedged per Seam C2) ===
#
# @code/beam.supervisor carries (children, strategy, policy);
# @magic/audit carries (audit_record, audit_strategy).
#
# The two compose-WITH the following mechanical glue (forward-promised):
#
# - supervisor.strategy reads from @magic/audit's audit_strategy
#   substrate vocabulary (landed at tick 11 consolidation per Seam C4).
# - For supervisor.children to mechanically hold contracts, supervisor
#   needs a `contract: magic_contract` field OR an action lift
#   `supervise_contract(s, c) -> supervisor` — neither has landed yet.
# - For audit_record to flow into supervisor decisions, `respond`
#   needs to consume a supervisor parameter or supervisor needs an
#   `audit_trail` field.
#
# Until those land, the @code/beam.supervisor ↔ @magic/audit
# composition is a recognition #81 promissory note. The substrate
# names the carriers; the mechanical glue is future work.
#
# === Spencer-Brown analogy (not inheritance) ===
#
# Per Seam C3: the previous tick inherited from
# @epistemologic/cybernetic/distinction via `in` clause AND claimed
# audit IS Spencer-Brown's mark at audit altitude. But cross takes
# (mark, distinction_space) and audit takes (magic_contract). Different
# types. The inheritance was decorative.
#
# Hedge: audit is ANALOGOUS to the mark at audit altitude; the
# distinction adapter species (when it lands) will provide the
# structural inheritance via `requires distinction_well_formed(...)`.
# Until then, no `in @epistemologic/cybernetic/distinction`.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   audit trail                 Accounting practice (centuries).
#                               The original tamper-evident record
#                               of a verifier's checks.
#   property-based testing      QuickCheck (Claessen-Hughes 2000).
#                               The property-level audit primitive
#                               in software verification.
#   supervisor behaviour        OTP supervisor (Armstrong et al.
#                               1996-2003). The Erlang/BEAM
#                               supervision-tree origin; @code/beam
#                               lifts this into substrate vocabulary.
#   Narcissus guardian          Per Void document
#                               [[corpus:void-dual-geometry]]: the
#                               Narcissus pole IS the structural
#                               immune system. @magic/audit IS the
#                               substrate's Narcissus-pole gatekeeper
#                               function (#78).
#
# Spec context: docs/math/the-tower/recognition-80-magic-as-form-
#               process-substrate-decl.md (Reed's scratch; the @magic
#               family this species closes operationally for
#               verification).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; audit is the alignment
#                       enforcement primitive),
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]]
#                       (transparency<audit_record> is the verdict
#                       carrier at the species boundary),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (all carriers
#                       typed).
# Related shards: magic.mirror (the family-root; declares the
#                  carriers this species composes),
#                 magic/contract.mirror (the verifier reads
#                  contract.honor's verdict; this species closes
#                  contract's operational gap),
#                 code/beam.mirror (the @code/beam.supervisor
#                  composes @magic/audit at supervision altitude;
#                  recognition #81 territory).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/magic/audit.mirror` declares `@magic/audit` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming/claessen-hughes-2000
source @arxiv/distributed/armstrong-2003

# === audit_strategy carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed variant per Seam C1+C4 (was stringly-typed `ref`
# with documented values at tick 10). The substrate-pull-correct
# enumeration of responses to a violation verdict; @code/beam.supervisor
# reads its strategy field from this canonical substrate vocabulary
# (Seam C4 de-BEAM closure).
#
# - `restart`    re-bind the contract with fresh state; honor
#                invariants from the bind altitude.
# - `escalate`   propagate the violation to the parent audit altitude.
# - `record`     add the violation to the audit trail; take no
#                enforcement action. Used for honest-trick @magic
#                (Splinter pole) where the contract is informational.
# - `enforce`    actively block the violating mechanism from
#                continuing. Used for con-detection @magic
#                (Narcissus-pole-as-guardian).
type audit_strategy = | restart | escalate | record | enforce

# === audit_record carrier ===
#
# A typed record per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming the tamper-
# evident outcome of an audit. Per Seam C1: verdict is typed against
# the substrate's transparency carrier (matching @magic/contract.honor's
# return type) rather than bare `ref`:
#
# - `contract`     the magic_contract that was audited.
# - `verdict`      transparency<magic_contract> verification outcome
#                  (success / partial(opacity_map) / failure(opacity_map);
#                  matches @magic/contract.honor's emit type).
# - `witness`      the witness ref naming what evidence the verdict
#                  rests on. KNOWN GAP per Seam: this is still a
#                  bare ref; sharpening to a structured witness type
#                  is forward-promised to a future tick (the witness
#                  type depends on which species the audit runs
#                  against; sharpening prematurely would over-fit).
# - `timestamp`    the temporal anchor (KNOWN GAP per Seam: should be
#                  the @kintsugi tick type when that lands; bare ref
#                  until then).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the quadruple.
type audit_record = {
  contract:  magic_contract,
  verdict:   transparency(magic_contract),
  witness:   ref,
  timestamp: ref,
}

# === audit action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary action that runs a verification on a
# contract and produces an audit_record. Composes contract.honor
# (reads the contract's current state) with the substrate's witness
# generation (records what evidence the verdict rests on).
#
# At Spencer-Brown altitude: audit IS the cross at @magic/audit;
# the mark distinguishes honored from violated; the audit_record IS
# the boundary the cross draws.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; per-species bodies
# discharge contract.honor and witness collection.
audit(c: magic_contract) -> audit_record { \ }

# === respond action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary action that applies an audit_strategy
# to an audit_record. The substrate-political enforcement step:
# given a violation verdict, apply the configured strategy.
#
# Composes with @code/beam.supervisor.swap_module at runtime
# altitude: a strategy=restart on a contract violation triggers
# the supervisor's swap_module to re-bind the contract under a
# fresh mechanism. Recognition #81 (candidate) names this
# composition.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
respond(r: audit_record, s: audit_strategy) -> audit_record { \ }

# === check_invariant action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary action that verifies a single named
# invariant against a contract, producing an audit_record scoped
# to that invariant. Stricter than audit (which runs the contract's
# full invariant set); used by downstream consumers that name
# specific properties.
#
# Returns audit_record so the witness carries the specific
# invariant verified.
check_invariant(c: magic_contract, inv: magic_invariant) -> audit_record { \ }

# === audited predicate ===
#
# Bilateral verdict predicate per recognition #37 (Pask agreement).
# Consumer shards name `requires audited(my_contract)` to declare
# bilateral agreement that their contract has been audited and the
# verdict is success.
#
# Same shape as contract.invariant_preserved, distinction's
# distinction_well_formed, eigenform's eigenform_witnessing. The
# bilateral commitment: the contract commits to declaring its
# invariant set; the consumer commits to running audit at the
# species boundary before consuming the contract's mechanism.
audited(c: magic_contract) -> verdict { \ }

out @magic/audit
out audit_record
out audit_strategy
out audit
out respond
out check_invariant
out audited
